{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And over the golden altar.</b> A different garment and a cover, to cover the holy things — namely the ark, the table, the menorah, the altars, and all the service vessels, such as knives, bowls, and pans."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The lemma reads 'a garment' followed by the critical notation צ\"ל אחד, indicating the correct reading should be 'one' (i.e., אחד), which then produces the reading אחד אחר ('one other')."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:15.551814752Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}